system-call numbers from <sys/syscall.h>: write 1, getpid 39
1. write(1, msg, 40) with the bare instruction:
hello from the bare syscall instruction
   bare instruction  : returned 40
2. write to descriptor 99, which is not open:
   bare instruction  : returned -9 (minus EBADF; EBADF is 9)
   libc write()      : returned -1, errno 9 (Bad file descriptor)
3. a system-call number the kernel does not have (1000):
   bare instruction  : returned -38 (minus ENOSYS; ENOSYS is 38)
   libc syscall(1000): returned -1, errno 38 (Function not implemented)
4. getpid three ways gives the same process id: yes
5. openat with mode 0640 as the fourth argument (in r10): file mode 640, as requested
